What happens if a diaper is too big?
What if you’re struggling to measure yourself?
Restricted blood flow can lead to tingling, numbness, or muscle cramps. Continuing to use tight diaper sizes may result in nerve or tissue damage and other serious health complications.
A diaper that makes indentations around the legs or waist could be a sign that you need to go up a size. If you spot redness around the groin area, that could also indicate a product that’s too tight.
The extra material from a diaper that’s too big has to go somewhere, and normally it’s around the buttocks. You may also find that the waist tends to sag, which leads to problems with diaper movement and can cause rustling sounds.
