As principal of Pilarcitos High School, an alternative school in Half Moon Bay, Bechar creates an alternative setting to meet the unique academic needs of every student. He advocates for Pilarcitos High at the district level, is a strong ally to students, and his first and primary purpose is to assist students in earning a high school diploma and building a plan for post secondary education.
Youth Leadership Institute has partnered with Pilarcitos High since January 2016 to establish a group for young people to be more engaged in their community. Principal Bechar was “very excited that students could learn 21st century skills such as critical thinking and collaboration, while developing real life skills such as public speaking and making a positive impact in their community.”
The San Mateo County Youth Commission was established in 1993 — a huge win for youth voice at local decision-making tables. A recognized entity of city government, Youth Commissions increase awareness of and advocate for youth issues, advise the Board of Supervisors, present policy recommendations, and create projects that serve the community.
In 2017-2018, the youth broke out into 5 committees to address the diverse issues facing San Mateo’s youth. They also organized and implemented the 2nd Annual Youth Summit, bringing together youth commissions from across the state to discuss key issues within their communities, share best practices, and formulate a vision for strengthening the network of youth leaders throughout California.
