The Story You Don’t Hear – Youth Leadership Institute
I live two blocks from Edison High School – it’s the only one on the southwest side of Fresno. It’s got a bad rap – people from the outside see it as a rough place where bad things happen.
A couple of my friends and family members were homeless for a time. For this reason, I’ve always had a thing about drugs – if I ever try it, if anything happens, that’s where I’ll end up.
I’ve been told that if I don’t do right, I’ll end up in one of four places: in jail, on the streets, still in high school at 25 years old, or in the grave. And it’s happened: a young person was gunned down at night for wearing the wrong sweater.
The consequences for my actions – whether or not they are “wrong” – are very real. I don’t do bad things, I don’t take drugs, but my face is this brown color, and the color of my sweater matters.
It’s time they have a voice – and a vote. ACA 8 will lower the voting age in California to 17 years old.
If passed, ACA 8 would lower the voting age in California to 17 years old. On August 14, it passed the Assembly Appropriations Committee and is now slated to hit the state house floor for a vote.
