Youth, Residents, and Fresno Building Healthy Communities Bring New Skate Park to South Fresno
Campaign Victories “Parks are worth the investment because children and families are worth the investment” – Antonio, Fresno Boys and Men of Color Youth Leader
This spring we are working towards the groundbreaking of a new skate park in south Fresno—where there exists a great need for more recreational space and where there is much fewer park space than in north Fresno.
BMOC Youth Leader Antonio Jauregui, who played an important role in this process, shared that many youth and Fresno residents do not have access to clean, safe parks. For Antonio, the closest, cleanest, and safest park is miles away from his home.
The struggle to bring park space was not without its challenges, as Sandra Celedon-Castro, Hub Manger of Fresno Building Healthy Communities, pointed out. One of the biggest challenges was securing all the necessary permits to finally break ground that day.
Additional speakers and adult allies included Fresno Parks Director Manuel Mollinedo and the Street League Skateboarding Foundation. Sher Moua closed the event by congratulating youth for their hard work: “This work is a reflection of the youth’s achievement.
The new skate park is scheduled to open in Spring 2016.
