How Loans Shape our Lives: The Story of My City Series – Youth Leadership Institute
How Loans Shape our Lives: The Story of My City Series
Student loans and owning credit cards can put people into more debt than they have ever known. Below, I discuss with Mercedians how their experiences with loans shape their lives.
I saw him struggle and I saw how he endeavoured through years and years of low-income. After that, I decided for myself that I’m not going to be like other people, I’m going to be frugal and live a good life by saving money and not going into debt.
When you look around, you see people with iPhones and expensive products that don’t need… What’s the point of spending so much on stuff you don’t need and live a terrible life?
Can you share how much money you have to pay off in loans?
If you could take one thing back from your college life involving money, what would you do?
I decided to attend UC Merced because they accepted me. UC Merced is one of the top schools for financial aid packages so that was a really big plus.
I have one credit card with my bank and another credit card with Target. Can you describe your experience with taking out loans, owning credit cards and buying things with money not in your pocket at UC Merced.
How much do you consider paying off debt when it comes to making money decisions and budgeting?
How much does your debt influence your career decisions? It doesn’t.
