I’m on My Way: An Interview with yli CEO Patty After a Decade of Service – Youth Leadership Institute
I’m on My Way: An Interview with yli CEO Patty After a Decade of Service
I was already getting good vibes through the application process and then got offered the position. And then, to actually build and work with a cohort of young people and allies on school climate in Marin County?
It’s an honor and a privilege to hear what people live at their deepest core, and the challenges they experience every day. I had the opportunity to see that transform into an understanding of their community’s experience, which then led to questions like, What are we going to do about it?
What’s the compelling data that we need to collect to tell this story in a really strategic way?
What are we going to do in those moments?
What do they support?
It was all strategy and timing. They’d say to the Supervisor, “Well, what do you think?
I never thought I would be sitting down with a local elected,” and “Why aren’t other young people doing this?” or “I didn’t think they’d listened to us.” I got to see, in real time, young people stepping into their power. They knew their stuff.
So, what do you want to leave behind at the 10 year mark?
What advice do you have for folks following in your footsteps?
