CHECK OUT OUR ANNUAL REPORT!
We Stand with the Dreamers
It is with conflicted heart that I write you in response to the ongoing politics in Washington, D.C. as it relates to the 800,000 young people who are part of Deferred Action for Childhood Arrivals (DACA). The truth is, DACA impacts all of us, regardless of our immigration status.
YLI stands unwaveringly on the side of our immigrant communities.
We know that this latest deal in Washington promises a vote on immigration policies nationally, and we are hopeful that a more permanent resolution will result from this agreement. We will be at the forefront of hope, demanding that our elected leaders in Congress and local communities create policies that protect you and enable you to continue on with your lives as we operate from a place of power, not panic.
Let us fight together to ensure all youth have a voice in our communities!
Please forward these to anyone who might need them!
Nationwide:Immigration Advocates Network/Non-Profit Resource Center
Women and Children:Immigration Center for Women and Children
We know that many of our partners are assisting with financial needs for those pursuing a renewal of their DACA, please reach out if you have questions. Additionally, if you or someone you know is searching for the Rapid Response Network lines, we would encourage you to save these resources:
Supreme Court Decisions Affect Real Lives – Youth Leadership Institute
With this lens, we were heartened earlier this week that the Supreme Court did not hasten a decision that would have put the DACA-mented community further at risk in the tenuous situation caused by the current administration.
The decision is infuriating, cruel, and not based in any real national concern. The Supreme Court’s decision to allow the ban to go forward while the cases work through the courts is gut wrenching and has profound impacts on real people.
We want to be clear – to our team members, young folks, and community members who identify as part of the trans and the gender non conforming community: We see you, we are listening, and we want to continue to be an organization that is home to, and grows and learns from, your experiences. We want you to know that your lived experience is valuable at YLI and that we are committed to working with you to create communities that feel the same.
Suspending Alcohol Licenses of Outlets Endangering Public Health – Youth Leadership Institute
The California Department of Alcoholic Beverage Control (ABC) has proposed an emergency rule that would allow them to issue immediate temporary suspensions of the licenses of any alcohol outlet engaging in gross violation of public health and safety. This is a direct response to alcohol licensees refusing to close or limit their businesses to prevent the spread of coronavirus.
