“You can’t really change your demand that sharply just because basically all of the can volume that is out there is practically spoken for,” Kingston said.
“There are very few manufacturers of aluminum cans in the United States. Beer producers have ordered about 11 percent more cans in the past year, so that’s an added squeeze on the supply of aluminum cans and can manufacturers just haven’t been able to keep up.”
