Laminated glass , also call multi-layer glass, is a super-safe glass, made by bonding two or more layers of glass to PVB, SGP, EVA , etc. Under high temperature and pressure to make them tightly stick together.
Multilayer laminated glass can effectively reduce noise . Due to the damping properties of the interlayer, it has a higher sound reduction index than a single piece of glass of equal thickness between 125 Hz and 4,000 Hz.
Laminated glass blocks more than 99% of the UV rays while allowing most of the visible light to pass, which protects the internals from fading. 4.
